WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
Let's make Leaf-and-twig insects.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:07.632
Use a twig body and leaf wings to make a butterfly, dragonfly or imaginary

3
00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:08.715
insect on paper.

4
00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:11.175
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:14.285
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:14.665 --> 00:00:16.910
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.970
An adult checks leaves and smooths or replaces sharp twig ends.

8
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.860
Use paper tape and crayons rather than loose tiny eyes.

9
00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:27.523
Step 1.

10
00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:29.788
Choose the insect pieces.

11
00:00:30.168 --> 00:00:32.943
Set the twig and four leaves beside the card.

12
00:00:33.323 --> 00:00:37.228
Choose two similar leaves for the top wings and two for the lower wings.

13
00:00:37.608 --> 00:00:40.088
A made-up insect can be any colour.

14
00:00:40.468 --> 00:00:41.848
Grown-up help.

15
00:00:42.228 --> 00:00:44.183
Check the natural pieces.

16
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:46.847
Step 2.

17
00:00:47.227 --> 00:00:48.587
Place the body.

18
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:51.297
Put the twig down the middle of the card.

19
00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:55.422
Use a short tape strip across each end to hold it to the card.

20
00:00:55.802 --> 00:00:58.262
Leave space on both sides for wings.

21
00:00:58.642 --> 00:01:00.022
Grown-up help.

22
00:01:00.402 --> 00:01:02.667
Help tape the twig securely.

23
00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.512
Step 3.

24
00:01:05.892 --> 00:01:07.192
Spread the wings.

25
00:01:07.572 --> 00:01:11.362
Place one pair of leaves on either side near the top of the twig.

26
00:01:11.742 --> 00:01:13.942
Put the second pair lower down.

27
00:01:14.322 --> 00:01:17.627
Try opening the wings wider before fixing them.

28
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.317
Step 4.

29
00:01:20.697 --> 00:01:22.162
Attach and draw.

30
00:01:22.542 --> 00:01:24.897
Tape each leaf stem to the card.

31
00:01:25.277 --> 00:01:28.257
Draw two antennae and a face near the top of the twig.

32
00:01:28.637 --> 00:01:33.108
Add six drawn legs if you want your insect to have the usual insect

33
00:01:33.108 --> 00:01:33.747
leg count.

34
00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.507
Grown-up help.

35
00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:37.727
Attach the leaves where needed.

36
00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:40.342
Step 5.

37
00:01:40.722 --> 00:01:42.757
Create its garden story.

38
00:01:43.137 --> 00:01:45.087
Give the insect a name.

39
00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:49.163
Draw a flower or a leaf beside it and describe what it might do

40
00:01:49.163 --> 00:01:49.427
there.

41
00:01:49.807 --> 00:01:52.942
Lay the picture flat to keep the leaves in place.

42
00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:54.702
Grown-up help.

43
00:01:55.082 --> 00:01:57.267
Check for loose twig or leaf pieces.

44
00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.582
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

45
00:02:01.962 --> 00:02:05.512
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

46
00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.912
Your creation can look different.

47
00:02:08.292 --> 00:02:12.107
Separate natural pieces from tape and card before sorting waste.

48
00:02:12.487 --> 00:02:15.092
Display flat indoors while leaves dry.

49
00:02:15.472 --> 00:02:17.432
They may curl or become brittle.

50
00:02:17.812 --> 00:02:18.802
Well done.

51
00:02:19.182 --> 00:02:21.612
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

